  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nElections - Bremer County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n Bremer County, Iowa\n \nElections\n \n \n\n \n\n Contact Benton County Elections\n \n \n\n \n \nHome\n \nVote\n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections\n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials\n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \nWelcome to the Bremer County Elections website.\n The Election Department in the Auditor’s Office is responsible for every aspect of conducting an election from voter registration to the final count of the votes. This site is designed to be a resource for residents looking to learn how to vote, find their elected officials, learn about becoming a candidate, or find past or upcoming election information.\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nQuick Links\n \nRegister to Vote\n \n Where Do I Vote?\n \nAm I Registered?\n \nHow Do I Vote?\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nBecome an Election Worker!\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nUpcoming & Recent Elections\n \n\n \n\n \nNov\n \n3\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election\n General Election \n\n Election Information Sample Ballot(s)\n Candidate List\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nJun\n \n2\n \n \n\n 2026 Primary Election\n Primary Election\n \n\n Statewide Results · Official Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nApr\n \n28\n \n \n\n City of Sumner City Council Vacancy\n Special Election\n \n\n Official Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n News\n \n\n NOTICE OF BOND ELECTION FOR SUMNER-FREDERICKSBURG SCHOOL DISTRICT\n \n\n\n\n\n NOTICE OF IN-PERSON ABSENTEE VOTING\n\n\nAll News\n \n \n\n \n FAQ\n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nCan I request an absentee ballot by email or fax?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nYes. You may request an absentee ballot via email or fax and a ballot will be mailed to you. However, in order for your ballot to be counted you must also mail in or drop off the original paper ballot request. \n\n \n\n \n \nAll Frequently Asked Questions\n \n \n\n \n Bremer County Voter Registration\n \n\n Updated October 15, 2026\n \n\n\n \nNo Party\n \n\n\n \n7,479\n \n\n \nRepublican\n \n\n\n \n6,394\n \n\n \nDemocratic\n \n\n\n \n3,977\n \n\n \nOther\n \n\n\n \n88\n \n\n \n \n \nTotal Registered Voters: 17,938\n \n Register to Vote\n \n \n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the Bremer County, Iowa, Elections website at https://bremercountyelections.iowa.gov.\n\n\n \n\n Address\n\n 415 E. Bremer Ave.\n \nWaverly, IA 50677\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n Bremer County Website\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n Monday - Friday\n \n8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. \n \nPhone\n\n (319) 352-0340 \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n"
